## MAJ

### MAJ-CORR-001: STATUS_MD + BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG existence pre-checks spurious for tooling slices

**Bug:** check-invocation-log-entry.sh unconditionally checks STATUS_MD and BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG file existence (lines 164-166 region) BEFORE cascade-status is parsed (lines 168-184). For tooling slices declaring `cascade-status: not applicable`, the script exits cleanly at line 229ish without reading either file. So both pre-checks are spurious — and worse, would falsely fail a tooling slice in a directory where those files happen to be missing.

**Fix:** in scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh, move the STATUS_MD and BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG existence checks INSIDE the onboarded / onboarded-operator-bump / blocked-on-adopter-conflict case branches where the files are actually consumed. The DISPATCH_NOTE existence check stays unconditional (DISPATCH-NOTE is read for ALL paths including not-applicable to extract the slice-type field).

Verify:
- onboarded reads BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG → check there
- onboarded-operator-bump reads BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG + STATUS_MD → check both there
- blocked-on-adopter-conflict reads BRANCH_PROTECTION_LOG (negative assertion) + DISPATCH-NOTE (TF ref) → check log there
- not-applicable reads neither → checks moved out

### MAJ-CORR-002: TF reference matching uses re.search() (first-match) instead of re.findall() + exactly-one assertion

**Bug:** TF reference matching for cascade-status=onboarded-operator-bump (lines 344-354) and cascade-status=blocked-on-adopter-conflict (lines 359-369) uses re.search() — returns first match, ignores duplicates. Review spec at fix-round-1 (cascade_status) + fix-round-5 (target_repo) ratified 'exactly-one-match assertion' as the canonical pattern (closes multi-occurrence injection bypasses). TF-reference matching missed this pattern application.

**Fix:** in scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh:
1. For onboarded-operator-bump TF-024X-renovate-<slug> match in STATUS.md: replace re.search() with re.findall(); assert len(matches) == 1; if 0 → exit 1 with 'no matching TF-024X-renovate row'; if ≥2 → exit 1 with 'expected exactly one TF-024X-renovate-<slug> match, found N: [list]'.
2. For blocked-on-adopter-conflict TF-024X-conflict-<adopter> match in DISPATCH-NOTE: same pattern. Replace re.search with re.findall + len==1 assertion.

In tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh add test cases:
- onboarded-operator-bump + STATUS.md has TWO matching TF-024X-renovate-<slug> lines (duplicates, copy-paste mistake, etc.) → exit 1 with 'found 2'
- blocked-on-adopter-conflict + DISPATCH-NOTE has TWO TF-024X-conflict-<adopter> references → exit 1 with 'found 2'

### R1-SAFE-MAJ-001 (7th re-litigation): NO action

**Disposition:** structurally closed at fix-round-12 via FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001. Reviewer correctly identifies that operator-supplied fields cannot fully prevent operator misuse; canonical defense is workflow-side wiring in 024B-extras. Recurring-class signal noted.

**Action:** none. Already FUP-tracked.

